{"name":"Silver Mine","hex":"#bec2c1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver mine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mine for silver ore."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver_mine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver mining","blocks":[{"text":"Silver mining is the extraction of silver by mining. Silver is a precious metal and holds high economic value. Because silver is often found in intimate combination with other metals, its extraction requires the use of complex technologies. In 2008, approximately 25,900 metric tons of silver were consumed worldwide, most of which came from mining. Silver mining has a variety of effects on the environment, humans, and animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Silberbergwerk_Suggental_Josephistollen.jpg/330px-Silberbergwerk_Suggental_Josephistollen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_mining","wikidata":"Q1048939"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver","wikidata":"Q1090"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)","wikidata":"Q317802"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/SilverOreUSGOV.jpg/500px-SilverOreUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/SilverOreUSGOV.jpg/500px-SilverOreUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A photograph of silver ore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilverOreUSGOV.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Giant_silver_nugget%21.png/500px-Giant_silver_nugget%21.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Giant_silver_nugget%21.png/1280px-Giant_silver_nugget%21.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Giant_silver_nugget%21.png/500px-Giant_silver_nugget%21.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A large nugget of native silver, mined in Colorado U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiant_silver_nugget!.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/EarlyAthenianCoin.jpg/500px-EarlyAthenianCoin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/EarlyAthenianCoin.jpg/500px-EarlyAthenianCoin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Early silver Athenian coin, 5th century BCE. British Museum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%